hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24217","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Farwah ibn Nawfal al-Ashja'i, from his father, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to me the daughter of Umm Salamah and said: You are only my foster father. He said: So he remained as long as Allah willed, then I came to him, and he said: What has the girl, or the little girl, done? He said: I said: She is with her mother. He said: Then what brings you, what have you come for? He said: I said: That you teach me what to say at my sleep. So he said: Recite at your sleep: Say, O you disbelievers. He said: Then sleep upon its seal, for it is a disavowal of polytheism."
